      "sample_index": 0,
      "text": "The edge length of a square can be expressed in two different ways, so we can set these two expressions equal to each other and solve for $x$:\n\\[4x-15=20-3x\\]\nAdding $3x$ to both sides and adding 15 to both sides gives:\n\\[7x=35\\]\nDividing both sides by 7 gives:\n\\[x=5\\]\nSubstituting $x=5$ into either expression for the edge length gives:\n\\[4(5)-15=5\\]\nSo the edge length of the square is 5 meters.\nThe area of a square is given by $s^2$, where $s$ is the length of one of its sides. So the area of the square is $5^2=\\boxed{25}$ square meters.\nThe answer is: 25",
