    {
      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "To find the area of the square, we need to first determine the length of its side. According to the problem, the length of the side of the square can be expressed in two different ways: \\(4x - 15\\) meters and \\(20 - 3x\\) meters. Since both expressions represent the same length, we can set them equal to each other and solve for \\(x\\):\n\n\\[\n4x - 15 = 20 - 3x\n\\]\n\nNext, we will solve this equation for \\(x\\):\n\n1. Add \\(3x\\) to both sides of the equation:\n\\[\n4x + 3x - 15 = 20\n\\]\n\n2. Simplify the left side:\n\\[\n7x - 15 = 20\n\\]\n\n3. Add 15 to both sides to isolate the term with \\(x\\):\n\\[\n7x = 35\n\\]\n\n4. Divide both sides by 7 to solve for \\(x\\):\n\\[\nx = 5\n\\]\n\nNow that we have \\(x = 5\\), we can substitute this value back into either expression for the side length to find the actual length of the side of the square. We'll use \\(4x - 15\\):\n\n\\[\n4(5) - 15 = 20 - 15 = 5 \\text{ meters}\n\\]\n\nSo, the length of the side of the square is 5 meters. To find the area of the square, we square the side length:\n\n\\[\n\\text{Area} = 5^2 = 25 \\text{ square meters}\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the area of the square is \\(\\boxed{25}\\) square meters.",
